<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Middle Elamite kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1100 BCE (approx.) · capital Susa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The classic age of Elam, when its kings built the ziggurat of Chogha Zanbil and carried off the law code of Hammurabi as plunder to Susa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the obscure end of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sukkalmah-dynasty">Sukkalmah dynasty</a>, a new line, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kidinuid-dynasty">Kidinuids</a>, ruled Susa and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-anshan">Anshan</a> from about 1500 BCE with the title 'king of Susa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">Anshan</a>'. From around 1400 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igihalkid-dynasty">Igihalkid dynasty</a> consolidated the kingdom, using Elamite rather than Akkadian for royal inscriptions and marrying into the Kassite royal house.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/untash-napirisha">Untash-Napirisha</a> built a new religious capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chogha-zanbil">Dur-Untash</a>, with the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziggurat">ziggurat</a> of Chogha Zanbil, dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inshushinak">Inshushinak</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napirisha">Napirisha</a>. In the 12th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shutrukid-dynasty">Shutrukid</a> kings made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> a military power: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shutruk-nahhunte">Shutruk-Nahhunte</a> I raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> in 1158 BCE and brought monuments including the stele of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin's</a> victory stele to Susa, where French excavators found them. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shilhak-inshushinak">Shilhak-Inshushinak</a> campaigned widely and left many glazed-brick inscriptions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1110 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-i">Nebuchadnezzar I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-dynasty-of-isin">Second Dynasty of Isin</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutelutush-inshushinak">Hutelutush-Inshushinak</a> and recovered the statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marduk">Marduk</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> then entered a poorly documented period until the rise of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/neo-elamite-kingdom">Neo-Elamite kingdom</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 BCE – 1100 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:29.85%;width:7.96%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1100 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Susa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Untash-Napirisha, Shutruk-Nahhunte I, Shilhak-Inshushinak</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Elamite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Elamite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Anshan and Susa, Igihalkid and Shutrukid dynasties</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1300&amp;focus=middle-elamite-kingdom" aria-label="Middle Elamite kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5921 1007 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Middle Elamite kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6241 1263L6241 1263M6241 1263L6241 1263"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6241 1263h0M6241 1263h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6241 1263h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6241 1263h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Susa. <a href="/atlas?year=-1300&amp;focus=middle-elamite-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
